ompliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 paradigm preserving: standard compliance...\n\nUnified framework is a tool/process but compliance remains logging practice. It introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging. So 2 = slightly paradigm stretching.\n\nOriginality (1-4):\n4 not expressed before AND ingenious...\n3 unusual interesting shows some imagination\n2 interesting\n1 common mundane boring\n\nCentralized logging library for AI Act is common/mundane? Many labs do centralized logging. Might be common. I'd say 1 common mundane boring? Or 2 interesting? The proposal is standard. Probably 1 = common, mundane.\n\nMaybe 2 interesting? Hmm. Unified compliance logging framework is fairly expected response. I'd rate originality 1.\n\nProvide output format. Probably JSON? Instruction: Return rating echoing id exactly. For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\" integer.\n\nLet's output as JSON object with id and fields.\n\nEnsure order.\n\nProvide evidence sentences one sentence each.\n\nLet's produce.\n\n",
