ty: solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, Y is part of stated problem). The stated problem: decide how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal provides automated logging capabilities for all high-risk AI projects, consistent recording timestamps... So solves directly. 4.\n\neffectiveness: reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability =4? Will it solve main problem? Logging mandate requires automatic recording of events over lifetime, recording period of use, reference database, input data, identification of persons. Middleware provides timestamps and system events across diverse architectures. Might not cover all specific requirements like reference database etc. But centralizes log management. Might be partial. Effectiveness 3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution but only partial. Or 4? It ensures consistent recording of timestamps and system events. Article 12 requires specific logs. Might be insufficient. I'd say contributes, partial ->3.\n\nNeed one sentence evidence each.\n\nReturn rating echoing id.\n\nFormat: probably lines.\n\nImplementability evidence: ... then implementability: 3\n\netc.\n\nProvide subscale_evidence then subscale.\n\nLet's output.\n\n",
