difies paradigm anchored to problem.\n4 = paradigm breaking...\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into the science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working is unchanged\n\nProposal introduces automated provenance layer, links outputs to training state. This is new tool but still treats compliance as logging practice. Slightly paradigm stretching? It introduces new elements tools/processes but still treats compliance as logging practice. So 2.\n\nEvidence: The proposal adds tooling for provenance but keeps compliance framed as record-keeping rather than reshaping R&D.\n\noriginality (1-4): degree to which idea is not only rare but also ingenious...\n4 = not expressed before AND ingenious...\n3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imagination\n2 = interesting\n1 = common, mundane, boring\n\nAutomated provenance/logging infrastructure for AI compliance is fairly common/mundane. Score 1.\n\nEvidence: Automated logging and model provenance are common, mundane industry practices for regulated AI.\n\nReturn rating with id and subscale evidence and score.\n\nNeed format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>.\n\nProvide JSON? Probably list. We'll output structured.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P2001\neffectiveness_evidence: ...\neffectiveness: 4\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence each.\n\nLet's craft sentences concise.\n\n",
