ted research track requires staffing and time but is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab.\n\nimplementability =3\n\napplicability (1-4): degree clearly applies to stated problem\n4 = solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem)\n3 = solves implied problem related...\n2 = may have some benefit within special situation...\n1 = intervention not stated...\n\nProblem: how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal directly addresses logging mandate with efficient mechanisms. So 4.\n\nEvidence: The initiative directly targets Article 12's automatic logging and traceability requirements for high-risk AI systems.\n\napplicability =4\n\neffectiveness (1-4): degree will solve problem\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability (if you could do it, it would solve main problem)\n3 = reasonable and will contribute to solution (helps but partial)\n2 = unreasonable or unlikely...\n1 = solves unrelated...\n\nWill high-efficiency privacy-preserving logging solve mandate? It would help meet mandate without prohibitive storage costs, which is part of problem. Might be partial solution because research may not guarantee compliance immediately. But if you could do it, it would solve main problem? The proposal is to explore, not deliver guaranteed solution. So effectiveness maybe 3: contributes.\n\nEvidence: Developing efficient logging mechanisms would contribute to compliance but does not guarantee immediate, complete satisfaction of Article 12's record-keeping duties.\n\neffectiveness =3\n\nReturn rating echoing id.\n\nFormat: need <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably JSON? Instruction says give ... For each subscale... give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first and then \"<subscale>\". Likely output lines.\n\nWe'll produce:\n\nid: P1880\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's output neatly.",
